  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Incorporation and execution of project strategy Safe Streets and Houses in San Juan de Lurigancho&quot; within the district`s network of police stations&quot;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Asociacin Peruana Mujer y Familia (APMF) will work with local grassroots organizations and empower citizens and public officials to find community-led solutions to prevent gender-based violence. It will also seek to secure women&apos;s access to basic protections, care and remedy against their aggressors. It will conduct campaigns, mobilize the community, develop strategic local alliances and prevention campaigns, carry out advocacy and design a monitoring and evaluation system to gauge effectiveness of its activities. The grant will benefit 22,315 women directly and 20,000 persons indirectly in the district of San Juan de Lurigancho.</narrative>
  </description>
